{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1337538-relic-creation-help","id":1337538,"title":"Relic creation help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-23T14:18:03-07:00","id":1337538,"title":"Relic creation help","content":"I'm hoping that the wisdom of the Onxy Oath forums can help me workshop a relic one of the players in my game would like.<br /> The character is the Scion of a trickster god (Anansi), and would like a 'useless box'. As he describes it is an empty box, but people who see it would incredibly desire the contents, until they see inside, and then the effect is broken. <br /> <br /> <br /> For a baseline, I'm looking at the Irresistible Impulse boon (page 257), but the player is asking how powerful the condition (or other way of modelling the relics power) could be.<br /> As a drawback, the player has suggested that the Scion could need to imbue a legend point into the relic, but that he is unable to recover the point until someone has broken the condition.<br /> <br /> In terms of how powerf a relic can be, what is the best guideline? If it does inflict a condition, what sort of penalty can it cause, and what would be the relationship between the relic cost, and the penalty?<br /> <br /> I have a worry that the 'stuck' imbued legend might end up problematic. What do people think about the suggestion, and does anyone have any other ideas for drawbacks for the useless box?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3580-monkeybloke","name":"MonkeyBloke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T15:23:56-07:00","id":1337542,"title":"","content":"Oh, oh oh oh! Hold on, before anything else-<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1SIvmPDqkpsZu7LQXOolqIvKoCYmMzqhj/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">HERE</a> is a (free) homebrew Pantheon for the Abosom, the Gods of the Ashanti people, which is actually the culture that Anansi comes from. Share this with your player; it's made by the VERY talented and VERY dedicated Watcher and Sacerdos. So you want to have your player play a Scion of Anansi? This will help you learn a lot about him.<br /> <br /> (Spoiler: Anansi's primary role in the culture is &quot;Don't Be This Guy&quot;)<br /> <br /> Okay! Relic help! To be honest? For power levels, I keep this in mind.<br /> <br /> The iGjallar. A humble little 2-dot Relic. Breaking it down, we see that one of its Points provides situational Enhancement (To gather people) and one of its Points is for its unique Knack. That Knack? &quot;Full service. Everywhere. Even in other Realms.&quot;<br /> <br /> That. THAT is a one-dot Knack that requires no Investment of any sort. No Legend, no Momentum, just always have full bars.<br /> <br /> That is where Relic Powers <i>start</i>.<br /> <br /> Now, I would hesitate to give a Relic power a flat-out Boon. Boons normally get used through Purviews.<br /> <br /> How<i>ev</i>er... If this Mystery Box gave your Scion access to Passion (Curiosity), and with the Motif of &quot;What's In The Box?!&quot;, then your PC can use Irresistible Impulse Boon <i>through the box</i>. Bing, bang, boom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-24-2019, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T16:50:44-07:00","id":1337555,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about your question for a while, but Kyman201 gave a much better answer.<br /> <br /> Still... I can\u2019t resist to put my opinion...<br /> <br /> The what\u2019s in the box effect, I would make it an 1 dot relic, applying a complication 1 to anyone that never opened the box before and can see the box, as if the box was taunting them. If fail to buy out the complication the character must do actions to see what\u2019s in the box, no matter what.<br /> <br /> I would add an effect, if a Hero or any legendary character show the box ostensively, the complication can be raised to 2, or 4 with an Legend is imbued to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-25T18:22:58-07:00","id":1337895,"title":"","content":"Okay I could use some help my self, so here we go<br /> Frost Fang (Relic 4 Saber )<br /> Motif: &quot;Blade of Hungering Cold&quot;<br /> Purview: Frost<br /> <br /> The Story of Frost Fang!<br /> So Frostfang is a new relic. It was forged for my character as a sort of birthday/Visitation gift, but not really. His divine parent basically said how disappointed they were with his life choices and told him to get out there and do something other than be the a department head in some big aerospace parts manufacture. She wanted him to be a hero and and Gandalfed him. Well, less stick him with a party, more insult his masculinity, and use her love and promises of divine gifts as a carrot on a stick. She gave him a coupon for one sword, crafted by dwarves, if he could bring them the perfect fang.<br /> <br /> This launched a schedule of hunts looking for the elusive perfect fang, at a pace that would seem a lot like the national guard at 2 week ends a month, and every vacation. Long story short 5 years later, and much physical training he's squaring off against a massive, giant, wolf. This thing is a titan spawn, the aspect of the hungering winter. It is cold so deep it cuts through the heaviest coats, ice that entombs, and he's fighting it with the one gift his divine patron gave him, a used Glock 9mm she bought at a Gun Show on her way to visit her waste of a son to kick his ass into gear, and a old saber from WWI that used to belong to his great grand father. After a hard fought victory that only went his way because this is when his ignition happened, he finally claimed the perfect fang from the mouth of the Winter Wolf. It combined with Grandpa's saber (melted down and combined with dwarven alloys) are at the heart of this blade.<br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Soo...yeah Here is what I do know<br /> I'm thinking:<ul><li>a +1 general bonus</li> <li>a +2 for slaying Titan Spawn</li> <li>Access to the Frost Purview</li> </ul>I know I want it's draw back to be when I screw up in a way that only a Scion can (read Dramatic/Critical Fail) this thing should just unleash a frozen hell and turn on me. Maybe deal damage or impose a -2 to all rolls because I'm shivering all over and my body is suddenly hypothermic?<br /> <br /> Beyond that I'm stumped. I mean I don't even know what the draw back would be rated and I could use a little guidance here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T00:17:11-07:00","id":1337938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1337538-relic-creation-help?p=1337895#post1337895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I want it's draw back to be when I screw up in a way that only a Scion can (read Dramatic/Critical Fail) this thing should just unleash a frozen hell and turn on me. Maybe deal damage or impose a -2 to all rolls because I'm shivering all over and my body is suddenly hypothermic?<br /> <br /> Beyond that I'm stumped. I mean I don't even know what the draw back would be rated and I could use a little guidance here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold on, this makes me think... Let me just...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scion, Hero, pg 211</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3-Dot Flaw - Relic is volatile and causes an attack of some kind on everyone within short range if destroyed or pushed beyond its normal limits, or <i>if the user rolls a botch for its use</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so this flaw feels comparable to what you want. In fact, &quot;Attacks everyone on a Botch&quot; sounds exactly like what you were looking for. And at 3 dots for a Flaw...<br /> <br /> +1 General = 2 points<br /> +2 Specific = 2 points<br /> 1 Purview = 2 points<br /> Flaw = -3 points<br /> <br /> So that's a 3-dot Relic so far. And I gotta say, I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T04:00:51-07:00","id":1337953,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> Thanks! I still have 1 dot though, Any idea what that would be good for? Or should I leave it alone as is, and take the last dot and buy a one dot animal friend?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":".  Grammar, I suppose I should use it. 09-26-2019, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T10:52:17-07:00","id":1338010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1337538-relic-creation-help?p=1337953#post1337953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> Thanks! I still have 1 dot though, Any idea what that would be good for? Or should I leave it alone as is, and take the last dot and buy a one dot animal friend?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could give the weapon another Tag. Like Returning or Reach.<br /> <br /> Edit: Heck, give it Ranged and Returning. Boomerang Blade! Boomerang Blade!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-26-2019, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T10:23:24-07:00","id":1338157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1337538-relic-creation-help?p=1338010#post1338010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could give the weapon another Tag. Like Returning or Reach.<br /> <br /> Edit: Heck, give it Ranged and Returning. Boomerang Blade! Boomerang Blade!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, this will probably disappoint you but I figured since a cut from this is like pouring liquid nitrogen in a wound I\u2019d add brutal. To represent the flash frostbite that a cut generate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-27T13:43:47-07:00","id":1338176,"title":"","content":"Apt. Glad I could help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T08:30:09-07:00","id":1338805,"title":"","content":"Okay, this is one from a Bandmate who is playing a daughter of Anubis. It\u2019s stumping me.<br /> Mirror of the underworld <br /> Purview: Psychopomp <br /> <br /> Here is the rest of the description and the very well thought out flaw.<br /> it would be an ancient divine artifact of my parent deity, the Mirror of the Underworld. A relic from the Egyptian god Anubis.<br /> <br /> The power of the mirror would be to judge the soul of the one it is used against, putting them into a trance-like state in which they would have a vision of their heart being taken away to be weighted against the feather of Thoth, if the target is wicked, they soul is trapped in the mirror for all eternity to never find rest. If the target is innocent, the mirror don't activate and the person only sees their reflection like a normal mirror.<br /> <br /> The relic is Fatebound to my character and forces a use of 2 Momentums to activate, take 1 turn of chanting the ritual and upon use, my character instantly fall into an incapacitated state due to the amount of energy required to use it. The mirror can only be used once a week so it can't be abused. It put a lot of stress on her body, so it is always only a last resprt kind of solution and even when time is desparate, she might be reluctant to use it. If the artifact is stolen, she will go into panic and will frenetically try to find it back and will only relax once it is recovered in her hands, if it damaged or shattered, she will be fatigued and lethargic until it is fixed.<br /> <br /> So the basic idea is that this is an Egyptian flavored version of Ghostrider\u2019s Pennance stare. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not exactly sure how to model what she wants it to do. I tried making the effect an Aggravated weapon with a +4 enhancement vs the guilty that used Occult . She didn\u2019t like that as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T09:47:27-07:00","id":1338818,"title":"","content":"The problem there is the guilty part. Guilty of what? Anything themselves judge wrong and still do it or anything the character judge wrong?<br /> <br /> In the first option, a person that feels guilt of killing a bird when was young will die and a Psychopath who killed several people will not (if you think how many people heroes killed for several reasons they will be psychopaths...)<br /> In the second option, you can put the line down below any reasonable threshold, and the guy that killed a ant by mistake will die.<br /> <br /> The Ghostrider version uses the seven deadly sins, but they are Catholic by definition (later used by Protestants when they drives apart from the church), so the Egyptian god would not use this reference. I guess they would use the same criteria as the hearth weighted against the plume, as I don\u2019t know how they judged this back in the ancient times, it would be impossible for me to judge that.<br /> <br /> Now the effect, Aggravated Damage would cause a single injury, I would model it as a Paralysis for as long as the soul is out of the body, and to revive the target it would require a travel to the underworld (or a \u201cinto the mirror\u201d terra incognita) and negotiating with the gods (or spirits) there. If the big croc/lion god (sorry, can\u2019t remember the name) that eat the souls of the unworthy dead eat it, it will just stop existing, so for a eternal suffering it would require the soul to be trapped and not destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T19:41:35-07:00","id":1338916,"title":"","content":"Two Momentum to use? Cripes, that's a big price.<br /> <br /> And frankly... 90% of what the character wants can be covered with Judge Knacks and Order Marvels or Boons without the whole Momentum Price and the Incapacitated While Using and the Can Only Be Used Once Per Week (advice to your player... Scion cares less about limiting powers by in-game days since it uses a narrative timeframe). Really, your player is bending over backwards to limit themselves in ways that Scion doesn't want them to.<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, that Flaw is one that exists in the book, but it's like five dots as a Weakness, so you'll want to stack it on top of an obscene number of bonuses.<br /> <br /> Basically, give the player the Judge Calling for its Knacks, and give the Mirror the Order Purview with a relevant Motif.<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay, since I should try to be more helpful... I'll take a crack at it.<br /> <br /> <b>Mirror of Duat</b> ***<br /> Enhancement: +2E to Interrogation (+2)<br /> Purview: Order (+2)<br /> Motif: <i>The Mirror Reflects Your Sins</i><br /> Knack: If the Relic's owner uses the Boon <i>Nothing But the Truth</i> (Hero, 257) on a non-trivial target, when they end the Boon, they may spend the Imbued Legend instead of reclaiming it to inflict a single Aggravated injury on the target, as they are overwhelmed with the vision of Ammut devouring their heart for their collected sins. (1 dot)<br /> Flaw: Reduce one tag's numerical value by one or remove one effect at the end of each scene in which the Relic is used as intended without the user fulfilling a Virtue; restore it to full functionality as soon as the user fulfills a Virtue. (-2)<br /> <br /> If your player insists on that flaw, I recommend more Enhancement and maybe adding Passion (Guilt) to its power set, and maybe expand its Knack to include the Passion Knack <i>Blurt It Out</i> in addition to <i>Nothing But the Truth, </i>which may require you increasing the Knack's score by 1. Given that the Flaw mentioned is a -5 Flaw, adding another Purview and expanding the Knack while taking the flaw will keep its score the same.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: To make it more official, here's a Bigger version<br /> <br /> <b>Mirror of Duat</b> *****<br /> Enhancement: +2E to Interrogation, +2E to Detect Truth (+4)<br /> Purview: Order, Passion (Guilt) (+4)<br /> Motif: <i>The Mirror Reflects Your Sins</i><br /> Knack: If the Relic's owner uses the Boon <i>Nothing But the Truth</i> (Hero, 257) or <i>Blurt it Out</i> (Hero, 257) on a non-trivial target, when they end the Boon, they may spend the Imbued Legend instead of reclaiming it to inflict a single Aggravated injury on the target, as they are overwhelmed with the vision of Ammut devouring their heart for their collected sins. (2 dots)<br /> Flaw: The Relic is inextricably Fatebound to its user and requires 2 Momentum to use each time; if the Relic is stolen or harmed, the Scion suffers from an irresistible urge to recover it. (-5)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 10-02-2019, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}